<title>USA: Economists divided on what action Fed will take.</title>
<headline>Economists divided on what action Fed will take.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economists were divided as to whether the Federal Reserve would inject reserves into the banking system or stay out of the market on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Economists were unsure as to whether the Fed had adequately met its current add need with Monday's seven-day fixed system repurchase agreements.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5.44 percent, slightly below the Fed's current official target level of 5-1/2 percent.</p>
<p>((  -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867 ))</p>
